      "prompt_version": "lean-to-tex-v3-strict-context-free-semantic-inputs",
      "tex_statement": "If $2\\le K<N$, $expect$ is a finite linear expectation, and expected 0-1 accuracy for each coordinate equals the expected posterior score for every choice rule, then for every $\\gamma$, posterior, and fidelity term, there exists an optimal rule $optRule$ maximizing the expected objective over all rules.",
